Notebook[{Cell["Graphical calculus \[Section]2.1.3: pivotal categories", 
   "Title", ExpressionUUID -> "c3095bc2-56c0-457c-85a3-480856462596"], 
  Cell["Turaev & Virelizier, Monoidal Categories and Topological Field \
Theory, pp. 33\[Dash]35 \[CenterDot] continues \
graphical-calculus-2.1-simplify.nb", "Subtitle", 
   ExpressionUUID -> "b4d62069-b17b-4cc6-8fbc-ac0db4090024"], 
  Cell["0. Setup", "Section", ExpressionUUID -> 
    "a59072f9-0ea1-4e4f-891e-a7f5fa27cb6f"], Cell["This notebook builds on \
the engine of graphical-calculus-2.1-simplify.nb: the StringDiagram data \
model, the layered form LD, level exchange (Figure 2.1), the rewrite rules \
and simplifyTrace. The first cell loads that notebook's code cells, so both \
notebooks must sit in the same folder (Desktop/Research/Monoidal Graphical \
Calculus).", "Text", ExpressionUUID -> 
    "1d385f4c-42ea-4a37-bd66-65183703434e"], Cell["ClearAll[\"Global`*\"];\n(\
* the \[Section]2.1.1\[Dash]2.1.2 engine: renderer, layered form, level \
exchange, rules, simplifyTrace, ... *)\nengineNotebook = \
FileNameJoin[{$HomeDirectory, \"Desktop\", \"Research\", \"Monoidal Graphical \
Calculus\", \"graphical-calculus-2.1-simplify.nb\"}];\n(* With (not Module): \
that notebook starts with ClearAll[\"Global`*\"], which would otherwise clear \
the loader's own variables *)\nWith[{cells = Cases[Get[engineNotebook], \
Cell[c_, \"Input\" | \"Code\", ___] :> c, Infinity], name = \
FileNameTake[engineNotebook]},\n \
Scan[Quiet@Check[TimeConstrained[ToExpression[#, StandardForm]; Null, 120], \
Null] &, cells];\n Print[\"Loaded \", Length[cells], \" code cells from \", \
name]];", "Input", ExpressionUUID -> "8584b321-d919-410f-bcde-641a03d833ad"], 
  Cell["1. Oriented arcs", "Section", ExpressionUUID -> 
    "b9676ec4-1de6-4bca-9e94-e9378596f99a"], Cell["In a pivotal category \
every arc carries an orientation. As in the book, diagrams read from bottom \
to top. An arc coloured X that points down contributes X to the source or \
target; an arc coloured X that points up contributes the dual X*. In the data \
the second case is simply the colour \"X*\", and the renderer draws it as an \
X arc with an upward arrow. Since an arc can be turned round, X** = X.", 
   "Text", ExpressionUUID -> "2f0f0f7e-e70a-4ca3-ac2b-fdbb8c26416f"], 
  Cell["The four duality morphisms of \[Section]1.7.1 are ev_X : X* \
\[CircleTimes] X \[RightArrow] \|01d7d9 and \:1ebdv_X : X \[CircleTimes] X* \
\[RightArrow] \|01d7d9 (the caps), and coev_X : \|01d7d9 \[RightArrow] X \
\[CircleTimes] X* and c\:0303oev_X : \|01d7d9 \[RightArrow] X* \[CircleTimes] \
X (the cups). In the data, \:1ebdv and c\:0303oev are written \"ev~\" and \
\"coev~\". The pair (\:1ebdv_X, c\:0303oev_X) is a non-degenerate pairing \
with its inverse, just like (ev_X, coev_X).", "Text", 
   ExpressionUUID -> "0048b374-335a-4a9c-9899-c37c827d4681"], 
  Cell["(* ===== Oriented arcs: the colour X (arrow down) and the colour X* \
(arrow up) ===== *)\nstarQ[c_String] := StringEndsQ[c, \"*\"];\nstarQ[_] := \
False;\nbaseC[c_String] := StringTrim[c, \"*\" ..];\ndualC[c_String] := \
If[starQ[c], StringDrop[c, -1], c <> \"*\"];   (* X** = X: the arc just turns \
round *)\ndualRow[cs_List] := Reverse[dualC /@ cs];                          \
(* (X \[CircleTimes] Y)* = Y* \[CircleTimes] X* *)\nstarName[s_String] := \
If[StringEndsQ[s, \"*\"], StringDrop[s, -1], s <> \"*\"];  (* f \
\[RightTeeArrow] f*, f* \[RightTeeArrow] f *)\n\n(* the four duality \
morphisms of \[Section]2.1.3 *)\nevP[x_] := B[Subscript[\"ev\", x], \
{dualC[x], x}, {}];          (* ev_X : X* \[CircleTimes] X \[RightArrow] \
\|01d7d9 *)\nevtP[x_] := B[Subscript[\"ev~\", x], {x, dualC[x]}, {}];        \
(* \:1ebdv_X : X \[CircleTimes] X* \[RightArrow] \|01d7d9 *)\ncoevP[x_] := \
B[Subscript[\"coev\", x], {}, {x, dualC[x]}];      (* coev_X : \|01d7d9 \
\[RightArrow] X \[CircleTimes] X* *)\ncoevtP[x_] := B[Subscript[\"coev~\", \
x], {}, {dualC[x], x}];    (* c\:0303oev_X : \|01d7d9 \[RightArrow] X* \
\[CircleTimes] X *)\ncapCupQ[s_] := MatchQ[s, Subscript[\"ev\" | \"ev~\" | \
\"coev\" | \"coev~\", _]];\n\n(* \:1ebdv_X and c\:0303oev_X form a second \
pairing and its inverse, so the (2.1) zigzags apply to them too \
*)\npairQ[Subscript[\"ev~\", x_], Subscript[\"coev~\", x_]] := True;\n\n(* \
typesetting: X* as X with a superscript star, \:1ebdv and c\:0303oev with \
tildes *)\ndispSym[s_String] /; starQ[s] && StringLength[s] > 1 := \
Superscript[dispSym[StringDrop[s, -1]], Style[\"*\", \
Plain]];\ndispSym[Subscript[\"ev~\", b_]] := Subscript[Style[\"e\\:0303v\", \
Plain], dispSym[b]];\ndispSym[Subscript[\"coev~\", b_]] := \
Subscript[Style[\"c\\:0303oev\", Plain], dispSym[b]];\n", "Input", 
   ExpressionUUID -> "2751f94f-6d7e-4eca-87ac-6c5ad6fc4250"], 
  Cell["2. Caps, cups and arrows", "Section", 
   ExpressionUUID -> "220e40d0-335d-41f7-a6c5-1075808c6ac3"], 
  Cell["The renderer of \[Section]2.1.2 is redefined so that every arc has an \
arrow and the four duality morphisms are drawn as caps and cups instead of \
boxes. Everything else (layout, labels, show, showEq, showTrace) is \
unchanged.", "Text", ExpressionUUID -> 
    "3d26ec63-a9ef-46ad-9544-785e2fede157"], Cell["(* ===== Renderer for \
\[Section]2.1.3: every arc carries an arrow, and ev, \:1ebdv, coev, \
c\:0303oev are caps and cups =====\n   As in the book, diagrams read from \
bottom to top. An arc coloured X points down and contributes X;\n   an arc \
coloured X* is drawn as an arc coloured X pointing up. *)\narrowHead[{x_, \
y_}, up_] := With[{s = If[up, 1, -1]},\n   Polygon[{{x - 0.07, y - 0.06 s}, \
{x + 0.07, y - 0.06 s}, {x, y + 0.07 s}}]];\nrender[d : StringDiagram[bs_, \
ws_]] := Module[{caps, plain, lines, boxes, arcs, pts, xr, yr, attached},\n   \
caps = Select[bs, capCupQ[#[[2]]] &];\n   plain = Complement[bs, caps];\n   \
attached[n_, edge_] := Sort[#[[2]] & /@ Select[ws, MemberQ[{#[[3]], #[[4]]}, \
edge[n]] &]];\n   lines = Table[With[{x = w[[2]], y1 = endY[d, w[[3]]], y2 = \
endY[d, w[[4]]], left = Length[w] > 4, c = w[[1]]},\n      {Black, \
AbsoluteThickness[2.4], Line[{{x, y1}, {x, y2}}],\n       If[c === unit, {}, \
arrowHead[{x, (y1 + y2)/2}, starQ[c]]],\n       \
Text[Style[dispSym[If[StringQ[c], baseC[c], c]], 12, FontFamily -> \
\"Times\"],\n        {x + If[left, -0.1, 0.1], labelY[w, y1, y2]}, {If[left, \
1, -1], 0}]}], {w, ws}];\n   arcs = Table[With[{xs = If[MatchQ[b[[2]], \
Subscript[\"ev\" | \"ev~\", _]], attached[b[[1]], BottomEdge], \
attached[b[[1]], TopEdge]],\n       cap = MatchQ[b[[2]], Subscript[\"ev\" | \
\"ev~\", _]]},\n      If[Length[xs] =!= 2, {},\n       {Black, \
AbsoluteThickness[2.4],\n        Circle[{Mean[xs], If[cap, b[[4]] - hgt/2, \
b[[4]] + hgt/2]}, {(xs[[2]] - xs[[1]])/2, hgt},\n         If[cap, {0, Pi}, \
{Pi, 2 Pi}]]}]], {b, caps}];\n   boxes = Table[{EdgeForm[{Black, \
AbsoluteThickness[1.2]}], White,\n      Rectangle[{b[[3, 1]], b[[4]] - \
hgt/2}, {b[[3, 2]], b[[4]] + hgt/2}], Black,\n      \
Text[Style[dispSym[b[[2]]], If[Head[b[[2]]] === Subscript, 13, 15], \
FontFamily -> \"Times\"],\n       {Mean[b[[3]]], b[[4]]}]}, {b, plain}];\n   \
pts = Join[Flatten[Table[{{w[[2]], endY[d, w[[3]]]}, {w[[2]], endY[d, \
w[[4]]]}}, {w, ws}], 1],\n     Flatten[Table[{{b[[3, 1]], b[[4]] - hgt}, \
{b[[3, 2]], b[[4]] + hgt}}, {b, bs}], 1]];\n   {xr, yr} = \
CoordinateBounds[pts];\n   yr = {Min[yr[[1]], -1], Max[yr[[2]], 1]};\n   \
Graphics[{lines, arcs, boxes}, PlotRange -> {xr + {-0.45, 0.45}, yr + {-0.1, \
0.1}},\n    ImageSize -> 62 (xr[[2]] - xr[[1]] + 0.9), BaselinePosition -> \
Axis]];\n", "Input", ExpressionUUID -> 
    "911c43ad-4ffc-42eb-9ba2-8770a4f0f666"], Cell["Page 34 of the book: the \
caps ev_X and \:1ebdv_X, the cups coev_X and c\:0303oev_X, id_{X*} as an \
upward X arc, and a box f : X* \[CircleTimes] Y \[RightArrow] U \
\[CircleTimes] V* \[CircleTimes] W.", "Text", 
   ExpressionUUID -> "c1354711-2e97-4df5-9323-d245255df05c"], 
  Cell["boxP[B[s_, i_, o_]] := LD[i, {{0, B[s, i, o]}}];\nColumn[{\n  \
Row[Riffle[Column[{render[fromLayered[boxP[#]]], Style[pretty[sym[#]], 14, \
FontFamily -> \"Times\"]}, Alignment -> Center] & /@\n     {evP[\"X\"], \
evtP[\"X\"], coevP[\"X\"], coevtP[\"X\"]}, \"      \"]],\n  \
Row[{show[fromLayered[idL[{\"X*\"}]]], \"        \", \
show[fromLayered[boxP[B[\"f\", {\"X*\", \"Y\"}, {\"U\", \"V*\", \
\"W\"}]]]]}]}, Spacings -> 2]", "Input", ExpressionUUID -> 
    "82865ad0-db06-4710-8635-2d5b4c6abdd9"], 
