    "1349de89-95b6-4179-a4d8-fdb809fba5d5"], Cell["8. Exercise 2.1.5", 
   "Section", ExpressionUUID -> "f99f5443-3aa5-4940-bdde-08d51eec86d9"], 
  Cell["Let \[Omega] : X \[CircleTimes] Y \[RightArrow] \|01d7d9 be a \
non-degenerate pairing with inverse \[CapitalOmega] : \|01d7d9 \[RightArrow] \
Y \[CircleTimes] X. The map \[CurlyPhi] : End(X) \[RightArrow] End(Y), f \
\[RightTeeArrow] (id_Y \[CircleTimes] \[Omega])(id_Y \[CircleTimes] f \
\[CircleTimes] id_Y)(\[CapitalOmega] \[CircleTimes] id_Y), is an \
anti-isomorphism of monoids with inverse \[Psi] : g \[RightTeeArrow] \
(\[Omega] \[CircleTimes] id_X)(id_X \[CircleTimes] g \[CircleTimes] \
id_X)(id_X \[CircleTimes] \[CapitalOmega]). The rules prove \
\[Psi](\[CurlyPhi](f)) = f, \[CurlyPhi](\[Psi](g)) = g and \[CurlyPhi](hf) = \
\[CurlyPhi](f)\[CurlyPhi](h).", "Text", ExpressionUUID -> 
    "5020d012-6cda-48b8-b847-c9960089d743"], Cell["phi[fl_LD] := \
stackL[stackL[besideL[boxL[\"\\[CapitalOmega]\", {}, {\"Y\", \"X\"}], \
idL[{\"Y\"}]], besideL[besideL[idL[{\"Y\"}], fl], idL[{\"Y\"}]]],\n   \
besideL[idL[{\"Y\"}], boxL[\"\\[Omega]\", {\"X\", \"Y\"}, {}]]];\npsi[gl_LD] \
:= stackL[stackL[besideL[idL[{\"X\"}], boxL[\"\\[CapitalOmega]\", {}, {\"Y\", \
\"X\"}]], besideL[besideL[idL[{\"X\"}], gl], idL[{\"X\"}]]],\n   \
besideL[boxL[\"\\[Omega]\", {\"X\", \"Y\"}, {}], idL[{\"X\"}]]];\nfE = \
boxL[\"f\", {\"X\"}, {\"X\"}]; hE = boxL[\"h\", {\"X\"}, {\"X\"}]; gE = \
boxL[\"g\", {\"Y\"}, {\"Y\"}];\nColumn[{showTrace[simplifyTrace[psi[phi[fE]], \
rulesP]], showTrace[simplifyTrace[phi[psi[gE]], rulesP]],\n  \
showEq[fromLayered /@ {phi[stackL[fE, hE]], stackL[phi[hE], phi[fE]]}]}, \
Spacings -> 3]", "Input", ExpressionUUID -> 
    "3ca0247a-5edc-4811-8d0a-5f6b56abb007"], 
