    "9efc1b9f-e07b-4227-b347-2ac67b6cc024"], Cell["9. Tests", "Section", 
   ExpressionUUID -> "7c5574a9-8350-4c4e-9d17-dac8fd186405"], 
  Cell["Every identity is checked twice: by the rules (sameQ) and in vector \
spaces, where X* is the dual space, ev and \:1ebdv are the pairing, coev and \
c\:0303oev are \[CapitalSigma] e_i \[CircleTimes] e_i*, and f* is the \
transpose of f.", "Text", ExpressionUUID -> 
    "b360ac48-cdd6-4330-8e8a-8cee311b1b5d"], Cell["SeedRandom[7];\nfMP = \
RandomInteger[{-3, 3}, {3, 2}];\ndimsP = <|\"X\" -> 2, \"Y\" -> 3, \"X*\" -> \
2, \"Y*\" -> 3|>;\nmatsP = <|\"f\" -> fMP, \"f*\" -> Transpose[fMP],\n   \
Subscript[\"ev\", \"X\"] -> {vec[2]}, Subscript[\"ev\", \"Y\"] -> {vec[3]}, \
Subscript[\"ev~\", \"X\"] -> {vec[2]}, Subscript[\"ev~\", \"Y\"] -> \
{vec[3]},\n   Subscript[\"coev\", \"X\"] -> Transpose[{vec[2]}], \
Subscript[\"coev\", \"Y\"] -> Transpose[{vec[3]}],\n   Subscript[\"coev~\", \
\"X\"] -> Transpose[{vec[2]}], Subscript[\"coev~\", \"Y\"] -> \
Transpose[{vec[3]}]|>;\nmat[ld_] := toMatrix[toExpression[fromLayered[ld]], \
dimsP, matsP];\ndiagsP = {fStarL, fStarR, z1, z2, z3, z4, d1L, d1R, d2L, d2R, \
d3L, d3R, d4L, d4R};\n<|\n \"Figure 2.2: the four zigzags reduce to \
identities\" -> (simplifyLD[#, rulesP] & /@ {z1, z2, z3, z4} === \
{idL[{\"X\"}], idL[{\"X\"}], idL[{\"X*\"}], idL[{\"X*\"}]}),\n \"Figure 2.2 \
in matrices\" -> (mat /@ {z1, z2, z3, z4} === \
ConstantArray[IdentityMatrix[2], 4]),\n \"Figure 2.3: both expressions fold \
to f*\" -> (simplifyLD[fStarL, rulesP] === simplifyLD[fStarR, rulesP] === \
fStar),\n \"Figure 2.3 in matrices\" -> (mat[fStarL] === mat[fStarR] === \
Transpose[fMP]),\n \"Figure 2.4 by the rules\" -> (sameQ[d1L, d1R, rulesP] && \
sameQ[d2L, d2R, rulesP] && sameQ[d3L, d3R, rulesP] && sameQ[d4L, d4R, \
rulesP]),\n \"Figure 2.4 in matrices\" -> (mat[d1L] === mat[d1R] && mat[d2L] \
=== mat[d2R] && mat[d3L] === mat[d3R] && mat[d4L] === mat[d4R]),\n \"every \
step keeps the matrix\" -> And @@ (Equal @@ (mat /@ (simplifyTrace[#, \
rulesP][[All, 2]])) & /@ diagsP),\n \"every layered form is valid\" -> And @@ \
(validQ[simplifyLD[#, rulesP]] & /@ diagsP),\n \"Exercise 2.1.5\" -> \
(simplifyLD[psi[phi[fE]], rulesP] === fE && simplifyLD[phi[psi[gE]], rulesP] \
=== gE &&\n    sameQ[phi[stackL[fE, hE]], stackL[phi[hE], phi[fE]], \
rulesP]),\n \"\[Section]2.1.2 results unchanged\" -> (sameQ[dfR, dfL] && \
sameQ[e1, e2] && sameQ[c1, c2] && sameQ[p1L, idY] && sameQ[p1R, idXb])\n|>", 
   "Input", ExpressionUUID -> "db18604b-a98f-45bc-a1c7-3c0d0762eeea"], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
      RowBox[
       {RowBox[{"\"Figure 2.2: the four zigzags reduce to identities\"", 
          "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", RowBox[{"\"Figure 2.2 in matrices\"", 
          "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", RowBox[
         {"\"Figure 2.3: both expressions fold to f*\"", "\[Rule]", "True"}], 
        ",", RowBox[{"\"Figure 2.3 in matrices\"", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"\"Figure 2.4 by the rules\"", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"\"Figure 2.4 in matrices\"", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"\"every step keeps the matrix\"", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"\"every layered form is valid\"", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"\"Exercise 2.1.5\"", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"\"\[Section]2.1.2 results unchanged\"", "\[Rule]", 
          "True"}]}], "\[RightAssociation]"}]], "Output", 
   ExpressionUUID -> "2b286b6b-0af8-4f2c-8ae6-7d66ea6cbf29"], 
  Cell["Appendix: implementation notes", "Section", 
   ExpressionUUID -> "f1f15d21-5cfc-48dc-8323-893cfe952d21"], 
  Cell["Colours: \"X\" is an arc coloured X pointing down; \"X*\" is an arc \
coloured X pointing up. dualC turns one into the other, so X** = X, as for an \
arc turned round. Box symbols follow the same convention: starName turns \
\"f\" into \"f*\" and \"f*\" back into \"f\".", "Item", 
   ExpressionUUID -> "0232bbe4-708b-4c16-96f5-e69700f8a841"], 
  Cell["Symbols: Subscript[\"ev\", X], Subscript[\"ev~\", X], \
Subscript[\"coev\", X], Subscript[\"coev~\", X]. The renderer draws them as \
caps and cups, and dispSym typesets the tildes.", "Item", 
   ExpressionUUID -> "fbac81f6-a2f6-4cae-b026-07cdea7c45f7"], 
  Cell["rulesP replaces the \[Or] rules of \[Section]2.1.2 (definition of \
\[Or]f, (2.2) slides) by their * versions and adds the right-hand ones for \
\:1ebdv and c\:0303oev. The original rules association is untouched, so the \
\[Section]2.1.2 notebook and its tests still work.", "Item", 
   ExpressionUUID -> "923bb8ee-5564-4344-9e37-2f44ff11c7d7"], 
  Cell["Rule direction: the folds read Figure 2.3 from right to left (three \
boxes become one), and the slides replace f* by f. Both sides of every Figure \
2.4 identity therefore reach the same normal form.", "Item", 
   ExpressionUUID -> "dd8bf875-fd3e-4c31-b89f-5e45fb0b9197"], 
  Cell["Limits carried over from \[Section]2.1.2: the folds only match three \
consecutive layers (after level exchange), and the monoidal constraint \
?*\:2082(X, Y) of page 35 is not drawn, because \[CircleTimes]-coloured \
strands are split into single colours.", "Item", 
   ExpressionUUID -> "67fca950-abed-48d3-97b1-db4f1d19f8f6"], 
  Cell["rulesPRightFirst tries the right zigzag first, like rulesRightFirst \
in \[Section]2.1.2.", "Item", ExpressionUUID -> 
    "72f04d0d-256f-4fb0-b49c-43b30243767c"], 
